# Build context hygiene. Most entries here are not about image size:
#
#   *.db*        — the learning database is the user's personal study history.
#                  Copying it into an image would bake one person's notes,
#                  mastery and vault into every container built from this repo.
#   server/vault — the content-addressed blob store: vault originals and the
#                  pictures and audio of every imported Anki deck. Hundreds of
#                  MB of the owner's own files, and `COPY server ./server` in
#                  the Dockerfile takes the whole directory.
#   .certs       — locally-trusted mkcert keys. The server serves HTTPS whenever
#                  they exist, so shipping them would both leak a private key and
#                  make the container serve TLS with a cert nobody else trusts.

node_modules
dist
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.githooks
.github

# Personal data — never in an image.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.db.pre-*.bak
server/*.db*
server/vault/
.certs
.env
.env.local

# The repo root, as an allowlist: shapes the image never needs are out, and the
# files the build does use are named back in. Anything new in the root is out by
# default rather than by an edit somebody has to remember.
*.csv
*.py
*.html
!index.html
*.json
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!tsconfig*.json

# Local scratch and tooling that has no business in a runtime image.
#
# `tools/` is NOT here, and that is deliberate. The BUILD stage runs
# `npm run build`, and vite.config.ts imports three files out of it
# (vite-plugin-sw.mjs, vite-plugin-compress.mjs, and precompress.mjs behind the
# second) — excluding the directory left them out of the context and the image
# build died with "Could not resolve ./tools/vite-plugin-sw.mjs", which reads as
# a missing dependency rather than as a context problem. Naming the three files
# back in one at a time is the same trap with a longer fuse: the fourth plugin
# somebody adds breaks the image again, and only at release time. The runtime
# stage copies server, dist, public and package.json by name, so nothing from
# tools/ reaches the shipped image either way.
temp/
docs/
demos/
.claude/
*.log

# Docs, kept out of the build context (the image does not serve them).
*.md
!README.md
